    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0341" n="243" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg243"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.71293/52: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-12T18:00:00-04:00">September 12, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>311. Department’s 291, August 27, 3 p.m.<anchor n="53" xml:id="d257-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Under date September 7, the Post Office Department issued orders
                        suspending parcel post service and money order business to and from
                        Manchuria, excepting Kwangtung Leased Territory. War Department is
                        suggesting to Philippines postal administration similar action.<anchor
                            n="54" xml:id="d257-f2"/></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>For the present at least, ordinary mail matter received in this country
                        bearing “Manchoukuo” postage is being delivered without penalty to the
                        addressee.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d257-f1" n="53" xml:id="d257-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d257-f2" n="54" xml:id="d257-f2-content">
                <p>On September 21, the War Department notified the Department of State that
                    Governor General of the Philippine Islands had reported the taking of similar
                    action there (811.71293/56).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
